<title>BRAZIL: Bradesco 1996 net 824 million reais.</title>
<headline>Bradesco 1996 net 824 million reais.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's largest private bank Bradesco sent to the stock exchange the following statement on 1996 results.</p>
<p>    shr			 0.87 real</p>
<p>    net			 824 million reais</p>
<p>    net worth		 5.460 bln reais</p>
<p>Bradesco's 1996 results were the highest ever announced by a Brazilian private company, according to analysts.</p>
<p>In the statement sent to the bolsa, Bradesco said it showed a 15.1 percent return on equity in 1996.</p>
<p>Total assets rose 17.97 percent to 38.766 billion reais, it said.</p>
<p>Bradesco said per-share earnings figures were provided in lots of 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>No comparative figures were available.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
